id: pm-ado-sdk-match-close-1025
title: Report SDK update match self-conflict during terminal transitions
description: "Historical SDK experiment: commitItemMutations mixed scalar plus terminal-status update with match on updated_at can reject its own internal close after the preliminary update advances the timestamp. The earlier matched scalar/status/agreement sequence is historical and does not establish isolation: updated_at permits ABA. Current NativeWriteFence uses forward-only ordinary SDK lifecycle writes, pre-dispatch current-field/native-history checks and post-dispatch foreign-history detection. A peer can still write between the final read and native update and an overlapping change may already be overwritten when ADO_CONFLICT is reported. Missing capability: a native monotonic expected-history compare-and-swap, tracked by pm-cli issues 1576 and 1620. Keep the original mixed-update self-conflict as a capability follow-up, never as a safe timestamp guard."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[1]: sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-25T16:01:14.931Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T00:27:20.765Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-ado-sdk-adoption
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T20:42:22.975Z",codex-agent,"Review correction: the initial scalar-update plus unguarded close workaround was unsafe and has been removed. Safe grouping now uses two commitItemMutations update operations in sequence, each matched to the preceding inspected/returned revision. The status-only update routes directly to one native close write; concurrent edits between steps refuse without overwriting them. The underlying SDK mixed-update self-match limitation remains for orchestrator reporting."
  "2026-10-26T03:49:20.920Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 ordering correction: the safe workaround needs scalars excluding agreement, then matched status-only native close, then matched ado_sync_base/ado_rev publication last. Publishing the closed base in the preliminary scalar commit was unsafe across SIGKILL. Native SDK close assignment clearing is retained and explicitly included in settled-value tests. The missing SDK contract remains a match consumed once for the whole mixed update, or BulkItemCloseMutation.match; no dependency bump or upstream write was made."
  "2026-11-02T00:27:20.765Z",codex-sol,"PR46 review clarification: updated the active description against pinned SDK 2026.10.27 and current code. Earlier comments/history remain historical evidence and do not describe the current safety policy."
